{"name":"Lush Un’goro Crater","hex":"#54a64d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Juicy, succulent.","Mellow; soft;  easily turned; fertile."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drunkard, sot, alcoholic.","Intoxicating liquor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lush"},{"term":"crater","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hemispherical pit created by the impact of a meteorite or other object. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The basin-like opening or mouth of a volcano, through which the chief eruption comes; similarly, the mouth of a geyser, about which a cone of silica is often built up."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form craters in a surface.","To collapse catastrophically; to become devastated or completely destroyed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crater","blocks":[{"text":"A crater is a landform consisting of a hole or depression on a planetary surface, usually caused either by an object hitting the surface, or by geological activity on the planet. A crater has classically been described as: \"a bowl-shaped pit that is formed by a volcano, an explosion, or a meteorite impact\". On Earth, craters are \"generally the result of volcanic eruptions\", while \"meteorite impact craters are common on the Moon, but are rare on Earth\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Barringer_Crater_aerial_photo_by_USGS.jpg/330px-Barringer_Crater_aerial_photo_by_USGS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crater","wikidata":"Q3240715"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Manicouagan-EO.JPG/500px-Manicouagan-EO.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Manicouagan-EO